ce on my index finger because this  phone is weighted more towards the top  because the camera bump it tends to lean  pretty quickly when I let go of my thumb  so that's just something I'm gonna have  to get used to whilst using this phone  on the plus side however the display is  phenomenal when I took it out of the box  one of the first things I did was go to  the settings display and change that  from 60 to 120 straight away full  disclosure I've never used a 120 her  refresh rate in a real in-depth kind of  review experience in the past I've  always been used to sixty hurt refresh  rates and I didn't think it was too much  of a big deal I thought my people just  made a huge deal of this it's the same  stuff  but when you actually have a phone in  your hand that has the ability to go  from 60 to 120 in the blink of an eye  and you can actually instantly notice  the difference there is a big difference  I've tried to screen record this which  is a fantastic new feature on the s20  happy about that one to display the  actual differences between 60 Hertz and  120 Hertz when you're in 60 Hertz mode  you might notice that it kind of  pixelated as you scroll up and down but  when you jump to 120 Hertz it's a lot  smoother a lot more fluid and kind of  more natural in a sense as a million-one  other people have already said when  you're in 120 Hertz mode unfortunately  you can't bump it up to the max  resolution that the Samsung S 20 ultra  can do you can only have this maximum  resolution on 63rd display mode now  Samsung has come out and said that's  because of a battery issue but it has  5000 amps in the battery so I don't know  personally I'd like to see that option  unlocked later down the track or even as  soon as they fix that okay  hunting mode that's really all I have  for you guys today the unboxing and the  first impressions are very very  important because you kind of get a  sense of what the phone's going to be  like next week I'm going to be putting  toget